    <item>
      <title>Catching up: From Spain to Bratislava (Again)</title>
      <link>https://miroadamy.com/posts/2026-08-28-from-spain-to-bratislava-again/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 28 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0200</pubDate>
      
      <guid>https://miroadamy.com/posts/2026-08-28-from-spain-to-bratislava-again/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;We always had this dream back in Canada: retire to Europe, &amp;ldquo;ideally somewhere south&amp;rdquo;. This post is about how that plan half-worked, twenty years early, and how it landed us in Bratislava instead.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;h2 class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;How Valencia actually happened (it was never a plan)&#xA;    &lt;div id=&#34;how-valencia-actually-happened-it-was-never-a-plan&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;    &lt;span&#xA;        class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none&#34;&gt;&#xA;        &lt;a class=&#34;text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline&#34; href=&#34;#how-valencia-actually-happened-it-was-never-a-plan&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/span&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;In 2012 we did our first ever trip to Spain (Madrid → Valencia → Barcelona), triggered by our daughter&amp;rsquo;s stay in Madrid. It was part of the student exchange where Silvia spent 3 months with a Spanish family in Madrid and we had a Spanish girl from that family with us in Ottawa. We loved the experience - it was different than Italy we knew, but intriguing. So we started to consider Spain as a possible retirement destination.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
    </item>
    
